  body: "# Family income attribution for JSA(IB) and Income Support\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    The captured chapter describes calculating and attributing income of specified family members for
    JSA(IB) or IS, while distinguishing joint claims and special rules involving an under-18 partner.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDo not apply this as a current rule for all children or all households.
    DMG 25007 carries a JSA/IS 64 memo call-out and a child-income cross-reference. JSA(Cont) is explicitly
    treated differently; polygamous-family provisions, chapter 30, transitional circumstances and current
    legal effects remain dependencies.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 25007, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25008, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25009, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n- [DMG 25004, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a800918ed915d74e622c16a/dmgch25.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 25: General rules on income.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch25`: PDF SHA-256 `39edc3ed8ee9c875eb68ce4cd4148194b23dbd23bb6444883a2f2cae90a75337`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `db488637a179cc93910c4e243381b5c961d6959ce72cd1d34aff14e403517e73`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsa-personal-rate
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The income chapter explicitly restricts its JSA(Cont) guidance to the claimant’s own
      earnings and excludes the family-income treatment used in JSA(IB)/IS.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch25/0004
      quote: "25004   The DM should follow the guidance in this Chapter when determining the amount of\n\
        \        a claimant's own earnings in a claim for JSA(Cont). The guidance on other income,\n \
        \       and the treatment of income of the members of the claimant's family does not apply\n \
        \       to a claim for JSA(Cont).\n\n        Note: For guidance on the treatment of occupational
        and personal pensions in\n        JSA(Cont) see DMG Chapter 23."
      locator: DMG 25004
  - target: term/jsais-income-assessment-period
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Attribution identifies whose income is considered; the period passage then identifies
      the separate dates and payment period needed to assess that income.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch25/0004
      quote: "25007   [See DMG Memo JSA/IS 64] In a claim for JSA(IB) or IS, the DM should calculate\n\
        \        the income of\n\n        1.    the claimant's partner and\n\n        2.    a child or
        young person who is a member of the claimant's family\n\n        in the same way as for the claimant1.
        This income should then be treated as the\n        claimant's income2. However DMs should consider
        if the circumstances in DMG"
      locator: DMG 25007
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch25/0007
      quote: "25031   To determine the period over which any income other than income from self-\n   \
        \     employment is taken into account the DM needs to establish\n\n        1.    the date of
        claim\n\n        2.    the first day of the claimant's benefit week (see DMG 25052 - 25054)\n\n\
        \        3.    the date on which the income is due to be paid (see DMG 25034 et seq)\n\n     \
        \   4.    the date on which the income is treated as paid (see DMG 25043 et seq) and\n\n     \
        \   5.    either1\n\n              5.1   the period for which the payment is made or\n\n     \
        \         5.2   the amount of\n\n                    5.2.a    JSA or IS that would be payable
        without the income and\n\n                    5.2.b    any disregard the DM would normally make
        on the weekly\n                             amount of the income.\n\n        See DMG Chapter 26
        on earnings disregards and DMG Chapter 28 on other\n        income with partial disregards.\n\n\
        \        Note 1: If the income is a payment of earnings when employment ends see DMG"
      locator: DMG 25031
